				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
						<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
						
					</div>
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha27" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><p class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwAg"><span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1" id="mwAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"none"}},"i":0}}]}'></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description" about="#mwt1"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_with_empty_Wikidata_description" about="#mwt1" id="mwBA"/></p>

<p id="mwBQ"><b id="mwBg">Water supply and sanitation in Taiwan</b> is characterized by uneven distribution of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Precipitation" title="Precipitation" id="mwBw">precipitation</a> and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Population_density" title="Population density" id="mwCA">dense population</a>.</p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCg"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg/250px-Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg/500px-Piston_Water_Pump_at_Yingfeng_DogRun_Area_20141014a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4928" data-file-height="3264" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCw"/></a><figcaption id="mwDA">Piston water pump at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yingfeng_Riverside_Park" title="Yingfeng Riverside Park" id="mwDQ">Yingfeng Riverside Park</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taipei" title="Taipei" id="mwDg">Taipei</a>.</figcaption></figure>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwDw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwEA" aria-labelledby="Water_resources"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Water_resources">Water resources</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Water_supply_and_sanitation_in_Taiwan&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Water resources"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwEQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zhuoshui_River,_Nantou_County_(Taiwan).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwEg"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zhuoshui_River,_Nantou_County_(Taiwan).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Zhuoshui_River%2C_Nantou_County_%28Taiwan%29.jpg/250px-Zhuoshui_River%2C_Nantou_County_%28Taiwan%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Zhuoshui_River%2C_Nantou_County_%28Taiwan%29.jpg/500px-Zhuoshui_River%2C_Nantou_County_%28Taiwan%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4928" data-file-height="3264" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwEw"/></a><figcaption id="mwFA">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhuoshui_River" title="Zhuoshui River" id="mwFQ">Zhuoshui River</a>, Taiwan's longest river, runs from east to west.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwFg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwFw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg/250px-Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg/500px-Bridges_across_Keelung_River_in_Chientan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4000" data-file-height="3000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwGA"/></a><figcaption id="mwGQ">An <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqueduct_(water_supply)" title="Aqueduct (water supply)" id="mwGg">aqueduct</a> across the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keelung_River" title="Keelung River" id="mwGw">Keelung River</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwHA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:东涌水库_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwHQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:东涌水库_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/%E4%B8%9C%E6%B6%8C%E6%B0%B4%E5%BA%93_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg/250px-%E4%B8%9C%E6%B6%8C%E6%B0%B4%E5%BA%93_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/%E4%B8%9C%E6%B6%8C%E6%B0%B4%E5%BA%93_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-%E4%B8%9C%E6%B6%8C%E6%B0%B4%E5%BA%93_-_Dongyong_Reservoir_-_2016.04_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3699" data-file-height="2774" data-file-type="bitmap" height="187" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwHg"/></a><figcaption id="mwHw">A reservoir in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dongyin" title="Dongyin" id="mwIA">Dongyin</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matsu_Islands" title="Matsu Islands" id="mwIQ">Lienchiang County</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwIg">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Mountain_Range" title="Central Mountain Range" id="mwIw">Central Mountain Range</a> is the main mountain range running from north to south of the island. Most of the rivers on the island flow from east to west following the contour of the mountains. Although the annual rainfall is up to 2,510<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwJA"> </span>mm, which is 2.5 times higher than the world's average, the distribution of the rainfall is not even due to the geographical condition of Taiwan.<sup about="#mwt4" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1" id="mwJQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKQ">In the period of 2000–2009, Taiwan had 95.07 billion tons of annual rain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Precipitation" title="Precipitation" id="mwKg">precipitation</a>. From there, 20.00 billion tons evaporated (21%), 70.10 billion tons became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surface_runoff" title="Surface runoff" id="mwKw">surface runoff</a> (74%) and 4.97 billion tons became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groundwater" title="Groundwater" id="mwLA">groundwater</a> (5%). Added from groundwater overdraft of 0.63 billion tons, the total groundwater pumping was 5.60 billion tons. From the surface runoff water, 54.70 billion tons was discharged to the sea, 4.35 billion tons became water supply for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_dams_and_reservoirs_in_Taiwan" title="List of dams and reservoirs in Taiwan" id="mwLQ">reservoirs</a> and 11.05 billion tons became river water diversion.<sup about="#mwt7" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-auto-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-2" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMg">Half of Taiwan's water is supplied by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typhoon" title="Typhoon" id="mwMw">typhoons</a>.<sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwNA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwOA" aria-labelledby="Water_scarcity"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Water_scarcity">Water scarcity</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Water_supply_and_sanitation_in_Taiwan&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Water scarcity"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwOQ">Despite its high annual rainfall, Taiwan is only able to use 20% of it as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_resource" title="Water resource" class="mw-redirect" id="mwOg">water resource</a>, making it in the 18th place under the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations" title="United Nations" id="mwOw">United Nations</a> global ranking in terms of being water resource poor region.<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwPA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwQA" aria-labelledby="Kinmen"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Kinmen">Kinmen</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Water_supply_and_sanitation_in_Taiwan&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Kinmen"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwQQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Jinjiang–Kinmen Pipeline"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt15" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt14" id="mwQg">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinjiang–Kinmen_Pipeline" title="Jinjiang–Kinmen Pipeline">Jinjiang–Kinmen Pipeline</a></div>
<p id="mwQw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinmen" title="Kinmen" id="mwRA">Kinmen</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_supply" title="Water supply" id="mwRQ">water supply</a> has been scarce over the past decades due to its shallow lakes, lack of rainfall and geographical constraints which makes building <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reservoir" title="Reservoir" id="mwRg">reservoirs</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dam" title="Dam" id="mwRw">dams</a> unfeasible. Water from reservoirs is barely enough to meet the demand during dry seasons. Therefore, Kinmen often <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overdrafting" title="Overdrafting" class="mw-redirect" id="mwSA">overuse</a> its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groundwater" title="Groundwater" id="mwSQ">groundwater</a> for up to 8,000 tonnes per day, causing rising <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidal_flood?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Tidal flood (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwSg" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Tidal flood"]}}'>tidal flood</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil_salinity" title="Soil salinity" id="mwSw">soil salinity</a>.<sup about="#mwt18" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwUA">In early September 2013 after Kinmen Deputy Commissioner <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_You-qin?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Wu You-qin (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwUQ" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Wu You-qin"]}}'>Wu You-qin</a> led a delegation to visit mainland China, the Chinese mainland government agreed to supply Kinmen with water from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinjiang,_Fujian" title="Jinjiang, Fujian" class="mw-redirect" id="mwUg">Jinjiang City</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujian" title="Fujian" id="mwUw">Fujian</a>. An undersea 16.7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwVA"> </span>km water pipeline will be built to carry water from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanmei_Reservoir?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Shanmei Reservoir (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwVQ" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Shanmei Reservoir"]}}'>Shanmei Reservoir</a> in Jinjiang city to coastal area of Kinmen. The pipeline is expected to deliver a maximum amount of 30,000 tonnes of water each day to Kinmen. A further 300 meter of water pipe will be constructed to a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_treatment" title="Water treatment" id="mwVg">water treatment plant</a>.<sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-6" id="mwVw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwWw">On 23–24 May 2015, Head of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Affairs_Office" title="Taiwan Affairs Office" id="mwXA">Taiwan Affairs Office</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Zhijun" title="Zhang Zhijun" id="mwXQ">Zhang Zhijun</a> visited Kinmen to discuss the water supply plan from Fujian to Kinmen. The initial stage is to supply 15,000 m<sup id="mwXg">3</sup> of fresh water a day, to be increased to 34,000 m<sup id="mwXw">3</sup> a day in the medium-term and to 55,000 m<sup id="mwYA">3</sup> in the long-term. The water company in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujian" title="Fujian" id="mwYQ">Fujian</a> will build a pumping station and pipeline to the coastal town of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bingzhou" title="Bingzhou" id="mwYg">Bingzhou</a> and the pipeline will be connected to a 17-km underground water pipeline to Tianpu in Kinmen which will cost NT$1.35 billion.<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwYw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZQ">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwZw" aria-labelledby="Water_consumption"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Water_consumption">Water consumption</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Water_supply_and_sanitation_in_Taiwan&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Water consumption"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwaA">The annual per capita water allowance is 4,000 m<sup id="mwaQ">3</sup> and the current average <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_footprint" title="Water footprint" id="mwag">water consumption</a> per capita in Taiwan is 271 liter per day.<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-theguardian_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"theguardian"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-theguardian-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-theguardian-8" id="mwaw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbQ">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2001, the annual water usage for Taiwan was 18,600 million tons, which was divided into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agriculture_in_Taiwan" title="Agriculture in Taiwan" id="mwcw">agriculture</a> (12,290 million tons), domestic (3,600 million tons), industry (1,750 million tons) and conservation (9,600 million tons).<sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mweA">Reservoir water supply, river water diversion and groundwater pumping made up the total water consumption for Taiwanese, which was 21.00 billion tons in total. Among them, 3.53 billion tons was used for household consumption (20%), 1.66 billion tons was used for industrial consumption (9%) and 15.81 billion tons was used for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agriculture_in_Taiwan" title="Agriculture in Taiwan" id="mweQ">agricultural</a> consumption.<sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-2" id="mweg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023 drought forced cuts to agricultural water consumption.<sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwgg" aria-labelledby="Institutions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Institutions">Institutions</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Water_supply_and_sanitation_in_Taiwan&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Institutions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwgw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:臺灣自來水公司總部.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwhA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:臺灣自來水公司總部.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/%E8%87%BA%E7%81%A3%E8%87%AA%E4%BE%86%E6%B0%B4%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E7%B8%BD%E9%83%A8.JPG/250px-%E8%87%BA%E7%81%A3%E8%87%AA%E4%BE%86%E6%B0%B4%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E7%B8%BD%E9%83%A8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/%E8%87%BA%E7%81%A3%E8%87%AA%E4%BE%86%E6%B0%B4%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E7%B8%BD%E9%83%A8.JPG/500px-%E8%87%BA%E7%81%A3%E8%87%AA%E4%BE%86%E6%B0%B4%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E7%B8%BD%E9%83%A8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1134" data-file-height="851" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwhQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwhg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Water_Corporation" title="Taiwan Water Corporation" id="mwhw">Taiwan Water Corporation</a> headquarters in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taichung" title="Taichung" id="mwiA">Taichung</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwiQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Water_Corporation" title="Taiwan Water Corporation" id="mwig">Taiwan Water Corporation</a> is the state-owned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_utility" title="Water utility" class="mw-redirect" id="mwiw">water utility</a> providing water supply to most of Taiwan.<sup about="#mwt40" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-water_12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"water"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-water-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-water-12" id="mwjA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

